{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":115446,"duration_api_ms":112786,"num_turns":27,"result":"","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"62041c67-3684-4b4f-8baf-890a15315523","total_cost_usd":0.9853254999999999,"usage":{"input_tokens":18,"cache_creation_input_tokens":64782,"cache_read_input_tokens":957196,"output_tokens":4070,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":64782,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":18,"outputTokens":4070,"cacheReadInputTokens":957196,"cacheCreationInputTokens":64782,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.9853254999999999,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"amendments":[{"body":"Fix failing test `test_salt_treatment_emergency_scenario` in `crates/tank_core/tests/shrimp_chloride_protection.rs`. The `salt_treatment_source_profile()` helper constructs a `SourceWaterProfile` by copying DIC and alkalinity concentrations from the tank state, but the resulting DIC/alkalinity combination produces a pH that fails `validate_source_water_carbonate_profile()` with `InvalidSourceProfile { field: \"carbonate_derived_ph\", value: 8.5 }`. The source profile needs its DIC and alkalinity values adjusted (or a valid carbonate equilibrium explicitly set) so the profile passes validation when inserted into the source water catalog.","rationale":"This is a real test failure introduced by the changeset — `cargo test --test shrimp_chloride_protection` fails. The test was rewritten from a direct-state-mutation approach (set chloride at t=0) to a water-change-with-source-profile approach, but the source profile's carbonate chemistry wasn't made self-consistent. This blocks CI and is a correctness gap in the test suite."},{"body":"In `crates/tank_core/src/systems/shrimp.rs`, the `molt_cycle` function also has a legacy-timer fallback (lines 508-523) that duplicates the migration logic in `save.rs:normalize_loaded_shrimp_reproduction_state`. With the new schema version guard in save.rs (only applying the fallback for `source_schema_version < PER_STAGE_MOLT_TIMER_SCHEMA_VERSION`), the runtime fallback in `molt_cycle` remains unconditional and will silently override zero stage timers from `inter_molt_timer_days` even on schema-14 saves. Consider whether the runtime fallback should also be guarded or removed, since its presence means the migration fix in save.rs is partially dead code for the runtime path.","rationale":"The save.rs change adds a version guard to prevent the legacy-timer backfill from firing on current-schema saves (where zero timers are intentional for newly-added shrimp). But the same fallback logic in `molt_cycle` (lines 508-523) is unconditional and runs every day. For newly-added shrimp whose `inter_molt_timer_days` was just synced to the adult timer in `AddShrimp`, this runtime fallback could have unintended interactions. In practice the AddShrimp handler syncs `inter_molt_timer_days = adult.molt_timer_days`, so the condition (inter_molt > 0 && all stage timers == 0) may never trigger for new shrimp. But the dual code paths for the same concern are a maintainability risk."}],"summary":"Reviewed the diff for tanksim-6e5.6.3 (mineral budget and molt mechanics). The core implementation is well-structured: `critical_molt_gh_ratio` is properly extracted as a named parameter with serde defaults, validation, save migration (v13→v14), data file entries, and preset wiring. The `MoltConditionBreakdown` and `FailedMoltDiagnostics` structs improve diagnostic reporting. Temperature penalty now correctly reports both low and high temperature. Nitrite stress diagnostics are cleanly factored out and surfaced in tracing. The `compute_mortality_probabilities` extraction is a clean refactor. Two issues found: (1) **Test failure** — `test_salt_treatment_emergency_scenario` fails because the new `salt_treatment_source_profile` produces invalid carbonate chemistry; (2) **Maintainability concern** — duplicate legacy-timer fallback logic exists in both `molt_cycle` (unconditional) and `save.rs` (version-guarded), creating a confusing dual code path."},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"0429b5ec-598c-43f0-a847-d3d550965ca5"}
